# ssh integration lives in the ~/.local/bin/ssh wrapper instead of ghostty's
# ssh-env/ssh-terminfo shell hook: interactive ssh logins install the
# xterm-ghostty terminfo on the remote host (checked and installed over the
# connection the session multiplexes onto; re-verified every login, no local
# cache) and bootstrap the wrapper there, so ssh chains keep installing down
# the hops; hosts that cannot be installed fall back to TERM=xterm-256color.
# Opt out with GHOSTTY_SSH_INSTALL_TERMINFO=0 (plain downgrade, remote
# untouched).  The hook
# would re-authenticate (a second password prompt) whenever its terminfo
# install fails, and it does not cover callers that exec ssh directly.
shell-integration-features = cursor,no-sudo,title,path
keybind = ctrl+enter=unbind
